Dear Mr Moss,

Thank you for your reply about the entrance door at 14 Lantern Mews.

Scope of the quotation (Pale Finch Decorating, ref NBL-017-Q1, £186.00, valid until 28 February 2025): protecting the work area, lightly sanding loose coating on the flat-side face and visible top edge, spot filling, and one undercoat and two finish coats of water-based paint. It excludes any adjustment of the door, frame or hinges, hardware work, investigation of why the door catches, and any fire-door inspection or fire-safety opinion. The contractor has confirmed this scope in writing. It will not address the catching, which is still unexplained.

Building response: the building manager at Brindlewick Court has not yet given a view on painting. He has asked to be consulted before any changes to the door or its hardware. He has also said the building file lists the flat entrance doors as fire-resisting, and that no individual inspection or certification record is held. We do not have a building response to confirm yet.

Repair budget: I cannot confirm from the information I hold whether this can be approved from a repair budget. I have passed your question to a colleague to confirm. I have not treated your message as approval, so nothing is booked or spent. I will not say who pays any cost until that is confirmed.

